OL,3,CProgramme listings for THU 4 DEC
OL,4,G2215FNight Tracks
OL,5,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,6,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,7,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,8,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,9,     Geverything in between.
OL,10,G2330F'Round Midnight
OL,11,     GRounding off his week, Venna
OL,12,     Gchooses to spotlight a release by
OL,13,     Ga saxophonist and producer that
OL,14,     Ghe has long been influenced by.
OL,15,G0030FThrough the Night
OL,16,     GThe Hungarian Radio Symphony
OL,17,     GOrchestra, Budapest plays
OL,18,     GMahler's tumultuous fifth
OL,19,     Gsymphony. In the first half of
OL,20,     Gthe concert Agnes Langer plays
OL,21,     GMozart's fourth violin concerto.
